cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the NILSS paper of Ni and Wang."
title: "nilss-jax: non-intrusive least squares shadowing in JAX, with reliability diagnostics"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Streaming, multi-parameter non-intrusive least squares shadowing (NILSS) for sensitivities of long-time averages of
  chaotic flows, written in JAX (automatic Jacobian-vector products, optional energy-surface constraint for Hamiltonian
  flows), with ensembles of runs, a reliability report that flags the failure signatures of shadowing in systems that
  are not uniformly hyperbolic, a finite-difference reference, and the vacuum Boozer-coordinate guiding-center flow as an
  application.
authors:
  - family-names: Ha
    given-names: Lin
repository-code: "https://github.com/BrianP2002/Guiding_Center_Optimizer"
keywords:
  - chaos
  - sensitivity analysis
  - shadowing
  - NILSS
  - JAX
  - guiding center
  - stellarator
